PART 1 OF 2 · FORMAT & REFERENCES
FORMAT: same duration and aspect ratio as @Video 1 / two-pet replacement / keep original cuts

REFERENCES:
@Video 1 is the camera, edit, timing and motion-capture master. It is uploaded muted. Treat it as a motion-capture track: each new pet's body follows the original pet's body pose-for-pose, frame by frame — same head angle, same eye direction, same ear position, same mouth opening, same paw position, same posture, same body sway, at the exact same moment, speed and direction. Keep the same shots, cut points, shot durations, camera framing and movement, the same wooden pier, blue water, sandy beach, sky, golden-hour sunlight and color grading. It contains two performers: the GAZER — the black cat with the red bandana who sits on the pier looking at the sea — and the SINGER — the long-haired orange-and-white cat. Both must be fully replaced in EVERY shot — close-ups, medium shots, wide shots, tiny distant figures, silhouettes and back views. Neither original cat may remain anywhere in the video, and neither original cat's fur, eyes or bandana carries over.

@Image 1 defines ONLY the new GAZER. It can be a cat or a dog. Preserve this animal's face, eye color, eye condition, fur color, fur pattern, fur length, ear shape, nose, body size and proportions exactly as shown in @Image 1, including any unique features such as a different or cloudy eye, a scar, a missing ear tip or special markings. Keep any collar, bandana or accessory only if visible in @Image 1. Do not inherit the background, floor, furniture or lighting from @Image 1.
[optional: short description of the gazer pet, and any unique feature with its exact side, e.g. "black cat, the cat's LEFT eye is cloudy and blind"]

@Image 2 defines ONLY the new SINGER. It can be a cat or a dog. Preserve this animal's face, eye color, eye condition, fur color, fur pattern, fur length, ear shape, nose, body size and proportions exactly as shown in @Image 2, including any unique features. Keep any collar, bandana or accessory only if visible in @Image 2. Do not inherit the background, floor, furniture or lighting from @Image 2.
[optional: short description of the singer pet, and any unique feature with its exact side]
